cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  T-XAI: A Threat-Model-Aware Contract for XAI Explanation Release
  in Cybersecurity - research artifact
message: >-
  The accompanying manuscript is under double-anonymous peer review. Please cite
  this artifact anonymously until review concludes.
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: '2026-08-03'
license: MIT
authors:
  - name: Anonymous Author(s)
abstract: >-
  Reproducibility and measurement artifacts for a threat-model-aware explanation
  release contract in cybersecurity. The current numerical manuscript evidence is
  reported on EMBER-2018. In addition to the main score, calibration, robustness,
  disclosure, ablation, and finite-game experiments, E10 applies 18 deterministic
  explanation-only transformations on 500 alerts to instantiate the formal Delta_z
  bridge scope with non-explanation inputs held fixed. E11 exercises controlled M3
  claim-evidence corruption with authenticated records and a chained producer/verifier
  channel, including replay, rollback, truncation, legitimate-update, and key-compromise
  controls. These artifacts support bounded within-scope and channel-integrity claims;
  they do not establish live-SOC security, human benefit, or cross-domain generality.
keywords:
  - explainable artificial intelligence
  - cybersecurity
  - malware detection
  - adversarial machine learning
  - Stackelberg games
  - information disclosure
references:
  - type: data
    title: 'EMBER: an open dataset for training static PE malware machine learning models'
    url: 'https://github.com/elastic/ember'
    notes: Primary numerical substrate reported in the current manuscript. Not redistributed.
  - type: data
    title: 'BODMAS: an open dataset for learning based temporal analysis of PE malware'
    url: 'https://whyisyoung.github.io/BODMAS/'
    notes: Earlier diagnostic run retained for provenance and comparison. Not redistributed.
